fix(dsc): make the shared-cache plan dump opt-in

The plan dump prints every cache file and every mapping on the happy
path.  Measured against the real 44-file cache with the kernel's own
format strings, that is 102 lines / 11,560 bytes: about 70% of the
16 KiB console ring, not the "~7 KiB" estimated in section 73.  The
ring drops the tail when it fills, which is exactly where dyld's
verdict, the exec diagnostics and the final failure end up.

Keep one summary line by default with the file/mapping count, mapped
bytes, extent, base, slide and whether the dynamic-config page was
appended.  Move the per-file/per-mapping table and the success-side
validation lines behind "kebab_dsc_verbose=1", default 0.

A rejected plan and a failed map still print their short reasons; they
now also dump the full plan detail when verbose is off, so a failure
keeps every value the verbose path would have shown.  The post-failure
shared_region_check_np probe is unchanged.

Measured (host renderer over the real cache, no hardware):
  plan dump:      102 lines / 11,560 bytes -> 1 line / 154 bytes
  map=1 happy:    118 lines / 13,294 bytes -> 6 lines / 652 bytes
  dry-run happy:  112 lines / 12,795 bytes -> 3 lines / 360 bytes

The 16 KiB ring is untouched.  Build: DEVELOPMENT/ARM64/KEBAB links;
kebab_dyldcache.c has the same warning set as before (four warnings
from included headers, none from this file).  No hardware; the board is
stranded.

